  {
   "id": "cap-bcl",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -900,
   "y": -1450,
   "width": 2600,
   "height": 64,
   "text": "routed experts 384×61 (FP4) **24.18B** (49.5%) · attention ×61 **18.29B** (37.4%) · shared expert + router ×61 **4.20B** (8.6%) · KV compressors ×61 **670.1M** (1.4%) · indexers ×30 **501.4M** (1.0%) · lm head **926.7M** (1.9%) · mHC mixers ×61 **84.0M** (0.2%) · embed **0** (row lookup) · DSpark ×3 **0** (only when drafting) · hash tables ×3 **0** (row lookup) · norms + mHC head **1.0M** (<0.1%)"
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-title",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -900,
   "y": -1300,
   "width": 1250,
   "height": 200,
   "text": "# DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813 — model  \nOne continuous stack L0–60, read top → bottom; layers that repeat are drawn once with **×N**. **Grey bars = tensors**, length ∝ channels per token (0.08 px/channel); stacked bars = the 4 mHC residual lanes. **Boxes = operations**, all one size; where parameters and compute live is the pair of bars above. T = sequence length. *Layer* tab = one decoder layer in detail."
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-legend",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 450,
   "y": -1300,
   "width": 1250,
   "height": 200,
   "text": "Every layer: 128 query heads over **one shared 512-dim KV head**; each query sees the last **128 raw tokens** (sliding window) plus **compressed KV** blocks.    \nRow colours — **cyan**: ÷4 compression (30 layers), a small indexer picks the top 1024 blocks · **grey**: ÷128 compression (31 layers), all blocks are read. MoE everywhere = 6 of 384 routed experts + 1 shared; L0–2 route by a fixed token-id table (hash). The barcode on the right lists every layer in order."
  },
  {
   "id": "raw1",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -980,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**raw text**  \"The cat sat…\"",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
